WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.720
Ai…

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.260
Why are you here?

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.420
C'mon, who do you think I am?

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.160
I wish you wouldn’t underestimate me.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:17.290
If you’re here, that means you infiltrated 
SOL's airplane 12,000 meters in the sky.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.630
Is the crew okay?

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.680
Okay?

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.320
You’re treating me like a bad guy.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.640
Look.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.940
Hayami!

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.940
She's just taking a nap.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.680
She's not hurt.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.420
Hand over SOL Technologies’s code key.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.700
Why are you doing this?

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.890
What will you do by taking over my company?

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:47.130
I want to use it.  Like this airplane.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:52.100
I control it.  Like this.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:59.040
If I want to, I can crash the plane.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.770
Are you threatening us?

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:04.960
C’mon, don’t glare at me.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.850
I’m not asking you to 
hand it over for free.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.150
I’ll give you a chance.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.280
Let’s duel for it.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.260
I may prove useful.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.530
What?  You’re still around?

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.200
We just had our emotional goodbyes!

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.830
But you keep coming back!

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.840
I’m the last one.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.540
I’ll use your previous duels as reference.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.810
Because you linked each other's data.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.550
Fine.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:48.150
I won't lose just because you 
know one or two of my duels.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.640
I'll give you a handicap.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.890
I'll take you on together!

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.410
We have no other options.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.410
That's right, Brother.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.300
Duel!

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:13.660
calling & feeling  I take your 
thoughts to heart  VRAINS

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:41.620
The data storm grazes my cheek, 
so I can't open my eyes

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:51.570
What are we trying to find?  
Where are we trying to go?

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.810
I won't make anyone sad anymore

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:05.350
I'll retrieve you  Let's go and look ahead

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:10.490
By meeting you, the world is in color

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:16.170
I'll protect you with an unseen bond

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.470
calling  With invisible wings

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:31.080
Destroy the dark and weakness within me

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.430
Since the duel has begun…

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.900
Playmaker!  Soulburner!  Revolver!

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.780
They're in a different location, 
so I linked them in.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.880
A duel's not exciting without a crowd.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.850
Ai, what are you doing?

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:58.420
You doing well, Playmaker?

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:03.210
You can’t interfere, 
so just watch the duel.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.990
Kusanagi, are you watching?

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:08.960
Ai…

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:16.060
Bro!  I'll watch your duel to learn!

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.300
That’s the spirit!

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:22.570
Everyone, enjoy our duel!

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:26.810
I will protect my brother!

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:29.050
Here I go!  My turn!

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:32.050
I summon Marincess Blue Tang!

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:38.990
When she’s summoned, I send a non-Blue 
Tang Marincess in my deck to the graveyard!

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.790
Link Summon!

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:45.480
Appear, Link 1 Marincess Blue Slug!

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:49.670
Blue Slug’s effect activates!

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:52.400
I add a Marincess in my graveyard to my hand!

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.140
Next, Blue Tang’s effect!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:59.380
Since I sent her to the graveyard 
to summon a Water Link Monster...

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:03.220
...I flip over the top 
three cards in my deck.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:07.590
And I add one Marincess 
card among them to my hand!

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:12.720
I Special Summon Sea Horse from my 
hand next to Blue Slug’s link!

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.730
Link Summon!

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:21.270
Appear, Link 2 Marincess Coral Anemone!

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.490
Coral Anemone’s effect!

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:28.890
She Special Summons Blue 
Slug next to her link!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.450
Shine!  The circuit of love and bonds!

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.190
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Water monsters!

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.320
Link Summon!

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:48.210
Awaken, Link 3 Marincess Marbled Rock!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.600
This is Aqua’s Marincess Deck.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:56.090
Next, Marbled Rock’s effect activates!

00:05:56.090 --> 00:06:00.560
I add a different Marincess card 
in my graveyard to my hand.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:05.410
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.320
Well done!

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:13.730
A Link 3 monster, two set cards 
and four cards in your hand.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:16.520
Your Marincess Deck is working great.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.990
Yes.  This is my most important deck.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.820
Well said.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.000
Aqua would be happy that 
you're using it so well.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.470
Now it’s my turn.

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:30.700
I draw!

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:35.810
I summon Pikari @Ignister from my hand!

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:43.930
Pikari’s effect activates!

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:47.190
I add Ignister AiLand 
from my deck to my hand!

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.330
Link Summon!

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:54.240
Appear, Link 1 Linguriboh!

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.660
I activate the Field Spell, Ignister AiLand!

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:04.140
I Special Summon a Level 4 or 
lower @Ignister from my hand!

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:07.280
Appear, Achichi @Ignister!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:13.950
Then Hiyari’s effect 
activates from my hand!

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:17.560
When there's a Link Monster 
in the Extra Monster Zone...

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:19.950
...I can Special Summon it next to its link!

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:23.370
Appear, Hiyari @Ignister!

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:29.890
Appear!  The circuit that guides the dark!

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:36.500
The summoning conditions are three Cyberses, 
which includes a Dark Attribute!

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.770
The creation of dark shadows!

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.360
The wisdom of the dark night 
scatters throughout the world!

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.040
Gather in my hand to become 
the power of rising vigor!

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.750
Link Summon!

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:53.610
Link 3 Dark Templar @Ignister!

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:57.700
Ignister AiLand’s effect!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:08:01.390
Appear, Doyon @Ignister!

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:08.430
Pikari @Ignister represents the 
feelings he has for Lightning.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:12.410
Achichi represents the 
feelings he has for Flame.

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:17.480
Hiyari represents the 
feelings he has for Aqua.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:22.050
And Doyon is Ai himself.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:23.780
Ai…

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.750
The cards for Ai and the vanished Ignis...

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:32.490
Ai's deck shows he cares for his friends.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:39.210
Brother, Ai is putting a lot into this duel.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:41.000
Please be careful.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.730
I know.

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.740
Doyon’s effect activates.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:48.710
I add Hiyari from my graveyard to my hand.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.710
Dark Templar’s effect activates!

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:56.600
When a monster is Special Summoned 
next to a Link Monster’s link...

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:03.420
...I Special Summon as many Level 4 or lower 
@Ignisters from my graveyard by negating their effects!

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:06.420
Come, Achichi and Pikari!

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.860
Appear!  The circuit that guides the dark!

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:18.010
The summoning conditions are at least two 
Cyberses, which includes a Fire Attribute!

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:25.940
With high spirits, the soul 
resurrects from the river of fire!

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.650
Become red hot and burn!

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:30.920
Link Summon!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:36.000
Appear, Link 3 Fire Phoenix @Ignister!

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:40.560
Fire Phoenix has appeared, as expected.

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:46.050
You’re claiming to know 
my strategies, Pandor?

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:47.900
Then how about this?

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:51.540
I’ll show you the strongest 
card that the Ignis have created.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:58.980
Since a Link Marker points towards the Spell 
& Trap Zone, I can activate a Link Spell.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:00.160
What?

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.980
Ai is using a Link Spell?

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.450
Can it be?

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:08.220
The three arrows that judge everything!

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:20.170
The Link Spell, Judgment Arrows!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.110
Ai used…

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:31.100
Judgment Arrows…

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.350
The card symbolizing the 
battle between the Ignis.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:38.550
Ai, you’re carrying 
on Lightning’s wishes?

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.550
He crossed the line.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:46.160
Ai, do you know what it means to use that?

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.640
You’re never coming back to us?

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:50.630
Come back?

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.520
How can I come back now?

00:10:55.520 --> 00:11:00.840
By the way, the girl named 
Miyu.  Was she saved?

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:06.140
Yes.  She's regained consciousness 
and is recovering.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:10.900
Aoi.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:13.720
Miyu!

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.560
Thank you.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.690
Aoi, you saved me, right?

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.800
Miyu!

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:28.500
Kusanagi’s brother was also saved, right?

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:30.470
Ai…

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:34.320
How great for you humans!

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:38.440
But my friends are all gone.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:40.840
That’s…

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.150
Sorry, Ai.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:47.220
Ai is taking this very seriously.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:52.160
Free will is the reflection 
of your friends and society.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:56.730
That's how you gradually toughen your spirit.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:12:01.540
Those who haven't toughened 
up can't control free will.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:06.700
He's been crushed by his own emotions.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.960
Don't worry, Blue Maiden.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:17.420
in his opponent, bringing the duel to his favor.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:20.790
C'mon, don't be so blunt.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:25.610
It shouldn't have said that.  Right, Bro?

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:29.790
Clever or a cutlet, all I have to do is win.
(Note: "Clever" and "cutlet" sound similar in Japanese.)

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:33.500
You made a pun using clever 
and cutlet?  That's meaty!

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:38.970
Cutlet and meaty?  You’re becoming smarter!

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.310
Thanks to you, Bro!

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.780
Here I go!  Battle!

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:48.750
Fire Phoenix attacks Marbled Rock!

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:52.300
Judgment Arrows’s effect doubles its ATK!

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:55.490
I won’t let you!

00:12:55.490 --> 00:12:58.320
Marbled Rock’s effect activates!

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:01.440
By sending a Marincess in 
my hand to the graveyard...

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:05.260
...she's not destroyed in 
battle, and damage becomes 0!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:09.250
Then I activate the trap 
card, Marincess Wave!

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:13.640
I negate Fire Phoenix’s effects 
until the end of the turn!

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:22.410
You stopped Fire Phoenix’s effect damage.

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:26.520
But I activate the Quick-Play 
Spell, TAimed Technique!

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:29.320
I banish Fire Phoenix from 
the Main Monster Zone.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:34.560
I banish a card from your hand for each of 
its Link Markers until the end of battle!

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:37.100
Fire Phoenix is Link 3.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:41.070
So all cards in your hand 
are banished, Blue Maiden.

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:49.770
Then Dark Templar moves from the Extra 
Monster Zone to the Main Monster Zone!

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:56.250
Without a hand, Marbled Rock’s destruction 
and damage negating effects can’t activate.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:58.980
You anticipated all this!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.260
Here I go!

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:03.180
Dark Templar attacks Marbled Rock!

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:07.190
Judgment Arrows’s effect!

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:10.160
Dark Templar’s ATK double!

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:18.040
Are you okay, Aoi?

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:20.640
Yes, Brother.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:23.120
I end my turn.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:26.640
And the banished Fire Phoenix returns.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:31.560
Your two banished cards 
also return to your hand.

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:35.590
Ai, can I ask you one thing?

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:43.360
You seem to feel responsible for 
failing to protect the other Ignis.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.930
But I feel the same.

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:49.880
I also couldn’t protect Aqua.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.380
You fought excellently.

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:56.240
I’m proud to be your partner.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:58.610
Thank you, Aqua.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:05.580
Why do we have to fight each other when 
we both suffered the same sadness?

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:10.020
Let’s stop this duel!

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:14.260
The same sadness?  How dare you!

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:17.020
What about that?

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.700
Isn’t Aqua supposed to be there?

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:25.770
Don’t worry about it.

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.210
I’m not trying to blame you.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:31.140
You and Aqua did fight together.

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.300
I know that well.

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:41.590
Ai, if you didn’t start this in the 
first place, I wouldn't need to exist.

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.550
How dare you.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.980
But that's fate.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:52.160
But I can say that time 
gradually moves forward.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:55.530
That's why I'm here instead of Aqua.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:16:00.200
Yeah, exactly!  I know that!

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:05.510
But for me, time has stopped moving!

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:16.750
Unless I defeat you with my own 
hands, I can’t move forward!

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.720
Ai…

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:27.830
Ai, by siding with the humans, you closed 
the Ignis's future with your own hands.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:31.070
I hope you don't regret it.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:34.540
Zaizen is next.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:42.090
What’s wrong?

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:43.960
Does your stomach hurt?

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:49.450
It’s true that humans created 
- and destroyed - the Ignis.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:52.460
And left you alone in the end.

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:59.700
Since SOL Technologies created the Ignis, 
as its employee, I want to apologize.

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:02.670
I’m very sorry.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.640
Brother?

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.600
Zaizen…

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.610
...apologized!

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:11.540
Zaizen…

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:17.640
But as an executive at SOL Technologies...

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:22.120
...my duty is to protect its thousands 
of employees and their families.

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:25.120
That’s why I can’t give you the code key!

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.860
Please back off, Ai!

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:30.520
So you also have something 
you want to protect.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:34.040
Then fight for those you protect!

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:36.400
I don’t need an apology!

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:39.470
Accept your fate and duel!

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.170
Your accusations are true.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.980
But it is what it is!

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:49.210
I'll stop you for those I protect!

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.340
Bring it on!

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:54.690
I'll judge you with Judgment Arrows!

00:17:57.150 --> 00:18:00.980
Two Link Monsters with 2300 ATK.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:07.330
During battle, Judgment Arrows 
will double their ATK.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:12.300
But unless we destroy them, we can’t win.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.040
My turn!  I draw!

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.510
I set a monster!

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:21.250
I activate the Continuous 
Spell, Stairs of Mail!

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:27.720
I send a Tindangle in my hand to the 
graveyard to switch a set monster to attack position!

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:30.720
I send Intruder to the graveyard!

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:35.060
Appear, Tindangle Angel!

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.380
Tindangle…

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:45.770
That deck uses set cards.  How troublesome.

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:48.170
Angel’s flip effect!

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:51.780
I can set a Flip Monster 
from my hand or graveyard.

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:55.900
Intruder’s effect activates 
from my graveyard!

00:18:55.900 --> 00:19:02.890
When a monster is Special Summoned and set 
on my field, I set this card from my graveyard.

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:07.120
Next, I Special Summon Tindangle Base Gardna!

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:13.100
When there's a set monster, I can Special 
Summon it from my hand in defense position!

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:16.570
The Continuous Spell, 
Stairs of Mail’s effect!

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:24.040
I send a Tindangle in my hand to the 
graveyard to switch my set monster to attack position!

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:27.040
Appear, Intruder!

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:30.650
Intruder’s effect activates!

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:35.650
When it’s flipped faceup, I add 
a Tindangle in my deck to my hand!

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:39.360
The Continuous Spell, 
Stairs of Mail’s effect!

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.360
Appear, Tindangle Hound!

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:47.800
Long time no see, scary pooch.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:51.300
Hound’s flip effect activates!

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:57.740
I select a monster, and Hound gains 
ATK equal to half its original ATK.

00:19:57.740 --> 00:20:00.540
Afterwards, the selected monster becomes set!

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:03.550
I select Intruder!

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:08.020
Hound gains 2200 ATK!

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:10.580
4700 ATK!

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:16.220
Now even if he uses Judgment Arrows, 
it has more ATK than @Ignister!

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:18.130
Which one will he attack?

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:22.500
Battle!  Hound attacks Dark Templar!

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:34.210
Ai!  You really won't back down?

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:38.950
Don’t get smug after just 100 damage!

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.920
It's not over yet!

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:41.950
Brother!

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:47.580
I activate the trap card, Marincess Decision!

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:53.450
I banish a Marincess from the graveyard to 
switch a set monster to defense position!

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:56.670
That monster’s effects 
don’t activate at this time.

00:20:56.670 --> 00:21:03.370
I banish Marincess Wave to switch 
Intruder to faceup defense position!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:12.080
And we can Link Summon by using the monster 
that was switched to defense position!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.530
Brother!

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:17.820
Open!  The circuit that unites us!

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:23.260
The summoning conditions 
are three Tindangles!

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.320
Link Summon!

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:42.280
Appear, Link 3!

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:46.750
Tindangle Acute Cerberus!

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:49.380
Zaizen Link Summoned!

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:52.180
So that’s Zaizen’s ace monster.

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:56.990
No, it’s their ace monster!  
Created from their bond!

00:21:56.990 --> 00:21:59.680
Sibling power, huh?

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.380
Show it to me!

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:09.620
I was told repeatedly

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:17.070
Only tales of dreams

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:24.040
Is my life precious?

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:27.040
Make up for  Make up for

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:34.540
The next sentimental

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:45.800
I'm not a machine

00:22:48.520 --> 00:22:52.240
I cry a single tear

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:57.470
A single answer moves me

00:22:58.630 --> 00:23:07.820
We helplessly sing for someone we can't reach

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:13.250
Are you ready?

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:18.600
Oh oh oh

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:23.830
Are you ready?

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:30.910
Are you ready?

00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:40.630
Ai tries to carry out his mission.

00:23:40.630 --> 00:23:43.730
And the sister tries to protect her brother.

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:48.220
They both have something to protect.

00:23:48.220 --> 00:23:53.880
Ai faces two opponents who are 
the complete opposite of him.

00:23:53.880 --> 00:24:00.680
He has nothing left to lose, so 
how will he feel after the battle?

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:04.610
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Wanting to Fight Each Other

00:24:04.610 --> 00:24:06.610
Into the VRAINS!
